{
  "abstract": "For every n and every primitive complex (2n+1)-th root of unity ζ, the permanent of the 2n × 2n matrix with entries 1 on the diagonal and (1 + ζ^(j−k))/(1 − ζ^(j−k)) off it equals 4^n (n!)^2/(2n+1). Zhi-Wei Sun posed the identity in OEIS A002454 (2022), and She, Sun and Xia proved it (arXiv:2208.12167, Theorem 1.3(ii)). The proof formalizes the determinant approach of Guo, Li, Tao and Wei.",
